    [Doc] Update GLM-5.3 guide with release images, tuning and 1M DCP (#18357)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Update the GLM-5.3 guide for the published `v0.30.0rc1-a3` and
    `v0.30.0rc1` images. Remove Experimental labels from the pages,
    navigation and translated titles, remove the obsolete early-access
    declaration, and update the model's support status.
    
    Add Chapter 9, Performance Tuning, following the GLM-5 and GLM-5.2
    guides: detailed node configurations, representative workloads from the
    supplied 0.30 RC performance reference, explicit optimization settings.
    
    Add a GLM-5.3 1M A3 PD/DCP example from the supplied configuration:
    Prefill DP2/TP16/DCP16 and Decode DP4/TP8/DCP8 across four nodes. Each
    node has its own script, followed by the grouped startup commands and
    proxy command. Fix the reference's shell assignments, select `glm47` for
    reasoning, expose the Prefill devices explicitly, and use the current
    `enable_mlapo` configuration option on Decode. Organize Chapter 5 into
    Context Below 1M and 1M Context Configuration, matching GLM-5.2. Align
    script indentation and startup command formatting, preserve the existing
    198K serving parameters, and fix the column count in the detailed node
    configuration table. Correct the MemCache setup link.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation only; no runtime code changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `python -m mkdocs build`: passed for both target branches; no link
    diagnostics for the changed GLM-5.3 guide. Existing diagnostics in other
    pages remain.
    - Markdownlint, codespell, translation catalog parsing, Python launcher
    parsing and `git diff --check`: passed.
    - Extracted the four new role scripts and checked them with `bash -n`.
    Ran the documented launcher with mocked processes, then evaluated the
    generated six rank invocations against a stub serving command. Verified
    devices, DP ranks, API ports, context parallel sizes, parsers and
    connector/optimization JSON.
    - Verified all ten new code blocks copy intact from the rendered HTML
    and checked the new and repaired anchors.
    - `bash format.sh ci` was attempted but stalled installing the
    actionlint environment on Windows and was stopped. The targeted
    documentation checks above completed.
    - No NPU serving or performance benchmark was run locally; the new
    example is based on the supplied configuration and does not introduce
    measured performance results.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/8cc9aa5ad350f6f80cf3bebb298d410803ff75a9
    
